  "body": "## What was broken\n\nA client thinking budget was written into `reasoning_effort`, a field Fireworks defines as a **string enum**. Measured against the real profile before the fix:\n\n```\nfireworks   budget_only -> {'reasoning_effort': 8192}\n```\n\nAn integer in an enum field. Any client asking for a specific thinking budget on Fireworks sent an invalid request. The profile also emitted `\"xhigh\"`, `\"max\"` and `\"none\"` — none of which appear in Fireworks' own API reference — and it held the only `budget_field=\"reasoning_effort\"` wiring in the codebase, with **zero tests** covering it.\n\n## Mechanism\n\n`NamedEffortReasoning.budget_field` writes the numeric budget into the named field. That is correct for LM Studio (`reasoning_tokens` is a real numeric field) and wrong for Fireworks, whose numeric path is a separate top-level object.\n\nPer [docs.fireworks.ai/guides/reasoning](https://docs.fireworks.ai/guides/reasoning), verified against the primary source:\n\n> \"You cannot specify both `thinking` and `reasoning_effort` in the same request. If both are provided, a validation error will be raised.\"\n\n```python\nthinking = {\"type\": \"enabled\", \"budget_tokens\": 4096}   # must be >= 1024\n```\n\n## The fix\n\nAdds `EffortOrThinkingBudgetReasoning`, a general encoder for gateways where a named-effort field and a numeric `thinking` object are mutually exclusive on the wire, and rewires Fireworks onto it:\n\n| Input | Emitted |\n| --- | --- |\n| effort | `reasoning_effort`, narrowed to `low\\|medium\\|high` (xhigh/max clamp to high) |\n| explicit budget | `thinking {type: enabled, budget_tokens: N}`, clamped up to 1024; `reasoning_effort` omitted |\n| reasoning off | `thinking {type: disabled}`; `reasoning_effort` omitted (was `\"none\"`) |\n\nThe two fields can never coexist **by construction** — each branch returns.\n\nNarrowing rather than widening is deliberate: an unsent reasoning field costs thinking on one provider, a wrongly-sent one fails every request, and Fireworks does not document what an unrecognised value does. Clamping up to the vendor's documented floor (rather than refusing) follows the existing clamp-non-interactively rule — our internal table maps MINIMAL/LOW to 512, which Fireworks would reject.\n\n`budget_field` is **kept** — `lmstudio/client.py:52` is a real user of it.\n\n## Verification\n\n23 new behavioural tests asserting the emitted body, including that the opposite key is **absent**, an invariant test across every policy shape, and one test against the live `OPENAI_CHAT_PROFILES[\"fireworks\"]` entry rather than a hand-copied table.\n\nMutation-tested — each guard confirmed failing by name:\n\n```\ndrop the clamp          -> only test_explicit_budget_below_floor_is_clamped_to_1024 failed\nwiden the effort map    -> only test_fireworks_profile_wires_..._encoder failed\nremove the OFF branch   -> only test_reasoning_off_sends_thinking_disabled... failed\n```\n\n```\ntests/providers            1050 passed, no regressions\nruff format --check        923 files already formatted\nruff check                 All checks passed!\nty check                   All checks passed!\n```\n\nIndependent probe over the real profile, 12 policy shapes, asserting no both-fields, no non-string effort, no undocumented value, no sub-floor budget:\n\n```\noff                        -> {'extra_body': {'thinking': {'type': 'disabled'}}}\non_bare                    -> {'reasoning_effort': 'high'}\nminimal / low              -> {'reasoning_effort': 'low'}\nmedium                     -> {'reasoning_effort': 'medium'}\nhigh / xhigh / max         -> {'reasoning_effort': 'high'}\nbudget_512                 -> {'extra_body': {'thinking': {'type': 'enabled', 'budget_tokens': 1024}}}\nbudget_8192                -> {'extra_body': {'thinking': {'type': 'enabled', 'budget_tokens': 8192}}}\nVIOLATIONS: none\n```\n\n## Not done\n\n**Per-model gating.** Fireworks does not document whether a non-reasoning model rejects or ignores `reasoning_effort`, and the codebase has no per-model capability data. Tracked separately.\n\n**No live key.** Every assertion here is against the emitted request body and the vendor's published contract — not a real Fireworks call. That distinction is deliberate and stated.\n\n## Residual risks\n\nThe `thinking {type: \"disabled\"}` form for turning reasoning off follows Fireworks' Anthropic-compatible `thinking` object, but the docs page shows only the `enabled` example — the disabled spelling is inferred from that convention. It replaces `reasoning_effort: \"none\"`, which was undocumented in the same way, so this is not a regression in confidence. Everything else is quoted from the vendor's own reference.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Y6SPhyApg7trDx44SJqNti\n",
