    "message": "fix(fireworks): send a documented reasoning wire shape\n\nA client thinking budget was written into `reasoning_effort`, which\nFireworks defines as a string enum. A budgeted request emitted\n`reasoning_effort: 8192` — an integer in an enum field — so any client\nasking for a specific thinking budget on Fireworks sent an invalid\nrequest. The profile also emitted \"xhigh\", \"max\" and \"none\", none of\nwhich appear in Fireworks' own API reference, and it carried the only\n`budget_field=\"reasoning_effort\"` wiring in the codebase with no test\ncovering it.\n\nMechanism: `NamedEffortReasoning.budget_field` writes the numeric budget\ninto the named field. That is correct for LM Studio (`reasoning_tokens`,\na real numeric field) and wrong for Fireworks, whose numeric path is a\nseparate top-level object. Per docs.fireworks.ai/guides/reasoning the\ntwo are mutually exclusive: \"You cannot specify both `thinking` and\n`reasoning_effort` in the same request. If both are provided, a\nvalidation error will be raised.\"\n\nThis adds `EffortOrThinkingBudgetReasoning`, a general encoder for\ngateways where a named-effort field and a numeric `thinking` object\ncannot coexist, and rewires the Fireworks profile onto it:\n\n  effort            -> reasoning_effort, narrowed to low|medium|high\n                       (xhigh and max clamp to high)\n  explicit budget   -> thinking {type: enabled, budget_tokens: N},\n                       clamped up to the documented floor of 1024,\n                       reasoning_effort omitted\n  reasoning off     -> thinking {type: disabled}, reasoning_effort\n                       omitted (was the undocumented \"none\")\n\nThe two fields can never coexist by construction — each branch returns.\nNarrowing rather than widening is deliberate: an unsent reasoning field\ncosts thinking on one provider, a wrongly-sent one fails every request,\nand Fireworks does not document what an unrecognised value does.\n\n`budget_field` is kept: `lmstudio/client.py:52` is a real user of it.\n\nVerification:\n- 23 new behavioural tests asserting the emitted body, including that\n  the opposite key is ABSENT, plus an invariant test over every policy\n  shape and one test against the live OPENAI_CHAT_PROFILES entry.\n- Mutation-tested: dropping the clamp killed only\n  test_explicit_budget_below_floor_is_clamped_to_1024; widening the\n  effort map killed only the profile-wiring test; removing the OFF\n  branch killed only the disabled-path test.\n- tests/providers full suite: 1050 passed, no regressions.\n- ruff format --check, ruff check, ty check: all clean.\n- An independent probe over the real profile across 12 policy shapes\n  reported zero invariant violations.\n\nNot done: per-model gating. Fireworks does not document whether a\nnon-reasoning model rejects or ignores `reasoning_effort`, and the\ncodebase has no per-model capability data. Tracked separately.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Y6SPhyApg7trDx44SJqNti",
